* START-HISTORY:
* 25 Oct 26 Windows port - from Linux fc4030a: "absolute" is _voc_ref's test (the separator, or a drive letter and colon) and an @SDSYS token in the
*               register path is expanded; Linux tested for a leading "/".  The kernel's acceptance (K$SHARED.REF) resolves with fullpath.
* 18 Oct 26 dm  New, S.66 (the shared account).  Called by _voc_ref when an OPEN of a name finds no entry in the account's own VOC, and by
*               list.shared.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    deffun shared_ref(name, fno, quiet) calling '!shared_ref'
*    ans = shared_ref(name, 2, @false)       ;* fno 2 the data file, 3 its dictionary
*    if ans # '' then pathname = ans<1> ; vflags = ans<2>
*
* Answers the pathname of the file and field 6 of its VOC entry in capitals, separated by a field mark, or nothing.  Nothing is the answer
* to every refusal; no message is given and no reason is told (a refused name is simply not there).
*
* THE ORDER OF THE CHECKS (each can only refuse):
*    1  The session: not the administrator (SDSYS reaches the files with LOGTO shared; its own OPEN does not follow them) and the session's
*       gate K$SHARED.READ is on.
*    2  The shape of the name: 1 to 63 characters, the first a lower case letter or a digit (so no name that begins with $ & ! * _ or %, which
*       keeps the system files $savedlists, $hold and the like, and every &...& file, out of reach), the rest lower case letters, digits
*       and . _ - $ (no colon, comma or space).  The name is folded to lower case first.
*    3  A name in the stock VOC (newvoc) is never looked up: md, sd.accounts and the like are the account's own.
*    4  The register record of the account called shared: it exists, is not suspended, and holds an absolute path.
*    5  The VOC of that account has the name (as given, lower case, upper case): an F entry, not a multifile.
*    6  Field 2 (field 3 for the dictionary) is the pathname: no @ token, taken from the shared account's directory when it is not absolute.
*    7  The name of shared's private catalogue directory.
*    8  The kernel (K$SHARED.REF) accepts the path: it exists, is strictly below the shared account's directory, and no part of it is a VOC,
*       a program file, a dictionary (except for the dictionary asked for) or the catalogue.
*    9  The first answer for a name in a session is audited:  shared open file=<name>.  The audit is written after the acceptance.
*
* quiet: 0 for a lookup.  Not 0 for LIST.SHARED, which shows what the accounts that hold the gate can reach: it skips step 1 (the
* administrator and the gate tests) and step 9 (the audit).  _voc_ref passes @false, so a lookup always makes the tests.
*
* It opens no file by name (only OPENPATH and a READ of what it opened), so it cannot call _voc_ref again.  Every file it opens is closed
* before it returns.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
function shared_ref(name, fno, quiet)
$catalog !shared_ref

$include int$keys.h
$include keys.h
$include err.h

   if not(quiet) then
      if kernel(K$ADMINISTRATOR, -1) then return ''
      if not(kernel(K$SHARED.READ, -1)) then return ''
   end

   if fno # 2 and fno # 3 then return ''

*  The shape of the name
   if len(name) < 1 or len(name) > 63 then return ''
   lname = downcase(name)
   letters = 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz'
   digits = '0123456789'
   if index(letters : digits, lname[1,1], 1) = 0 then return ''
   shape.ok = @true
   for ch = 2 to len(lname)
      if index(letters : digits : '._-$', lname[ch,1], 1) = 0 then shape.ok = @false
   next ch
   if not(shape.ok) then return ''

*  The stock names are never looked up
   openpath @sdsys:@ds:'newvoc' to stock.f else return ''
   read stock.rec from stock.f, lname then
      close stock.f
      return ''
   end
   close stock.f

*  The register record of the shared account
   openpath @sdsys:@ds:'accounts' to acc.f else return ''
   read acc.rec from acc.f, 'shared' else
      close acc.f
      return ''
   end
   close acc.f
   if upcase(trim(acc.rec<ACC$SUSPENDED>)) = 'SUSPENDED' then return ''
   spath = acc.rec<ACC$PATH>
*  25 Oct 26 Windows port: the register holds a Windows path (drive letter, or an @SDSYS token), not a path that begins with the separator;
*  "absolute" is the test _voc_ref makes.
   if spath[1,1] = '@' then spath = parse.pathname.tokens(spath)
   if len(spath) < 2 then return ''
*  26 Oct 26 RELEASE_1.1 189: CREATE.ACCOUNT writes the register path with forward slashes (C:/ProgramData/SD/group_accounts/shared), which the old test refused,
*  so on a fresh install the shared account was in no session's reach and LIST.SHARED said there was none.  A drive letter with either slash is absolute.
   if not(spath matches "'":@ds:"'0X":@vm:"1A':\'0X":@vm:"1A':/'0X") then return ''

*  The entry of shared's own VOC, and the name of its private catalogue; the same three folds as _voc_ref
   openpath spath:@ds:'voc' to svoc else return ''
   found = @false
   rec = ''
   read rec from svoc, name then
      found = @true
   end else
      read rec from svoc, lname then
         found = @true
      end else
         read rec from svoc, upcase(name) then
            found = @true
         end
      end
   end

   catname = 'cat'
   crec = ''
   read crec from svoc, '$private.catalogue' else
      read crec from svoc, '$PRIVATE.CATALOGUE' else crec = ''
   end
   close svoc
   if upcase(crec[1,1]) = 'X' then catname = crec<2>
   if catname = '' then catname = 'cat'

   if not(found) then return ''
   if upcase(rec[1,1]) # 'F' then return ''
   if rec<4> # '' then return ''           ;* a multifile

*  The path
   p = rec<fno>
   if p = '' then return ''
   if p[1,1] = '@' then return ''          ;* no token expansion
   if not(p matches "'":@ds:"'0X":@vm:"1A':\'0X":@vm:"1A':/'0X") then p = spath : @ds : p     ;* 25 Oct 26 Windows port: as _voc_ref's "make pathname absolute"

*  The kernel's acceptance: inside shared's directory, and no VOC, program file, dictionary (but the one asked for) or catalogue on the way
   if not(kernel(K$SHARED.REF, p : @fm : fno : @fm : catname)) then return ''

*  One audit line for each name in a session, after the name has been accepted
   if not(quiet) then
      if kernel(K$SHARED.ONCE, lname) then
         void kernel(K$AUDIT, 'shared open file=' : lname)
      end
   end

   return p : @fm : upcase(rec<6>)
end

* END-CODE
